      "writtenOn": "2023-02-15T02:16:54Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure that\u0027s the issue. Xivu also does not call `tcpc_alert_event` and I\u0027ve personally verified tcpc charging is working properly on it. The new tcpc driver should be calling `schedule_deferred_pd_interrupt` on the board\u0027s behalf. I suspect the problem might be because yaviks partially uses chip specific code for its tcpc interrupt and the common driver is not working properly with it. I\u0027ve submitted a temporary work around by adding an exception to yaviks to not use the common tcpc driver until I can find a fix.",
